  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## B3 (cont.): theta-scaling at theta = (1,0), symbolic-phi series, cross-checks",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "checks = Join[checks, ck]; ck = <||>;\nck[\"B3 numeric: all (rep,branch,phi-point): eigen-equations exact\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[ckB[k][\"eig\"], {k, Keys[ckB]}]];\nck[\"B3 numeric: eps^0 = W4 untwisted data\"] = And @@ Table[ckB[k][\"ord0\"], {k, Keys[ckB]}];\nck[\"B3 numeric: H1+H2 = sum_{i!=j} zeta_i mu_j (order 1 only), all orders to nMaxN\"] = And @@ Table[ckB[k][\"HsumRule\"], {k, Keys[ckB]}];\nck[\"B3 numeric: no-log relation (b=a(H-a)/c2 for [2,1,0],[3,1,0]; quadratic D2 relation for [3,2,0]) both sites, all orders\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[ckB[k][\"rel\"], {k, Keys[ckB]}]];\nck[\"B3 numeric: b1+b2 = eps^2 (phi1 phi2 mu3 + phi1 phi3 mu2 + phi2 phi3 mu1), exactly, all orders\"] = And @@ Table[ckB[k][\"bsumRule\"], {k, Keys[ckB]}];\n(* theta scaling: H_n, a_n ~ th12^(n-1), b_n ~ th12^(n-2); compare with theta = (1,0) (th12 = 1) *)\nDo[Module[{b = k[[2]], Lam = k[[1]], r1, r2, pp = k[[3]], ph, ok},\n  ph = If[pp == \"A\", phiA, phiB];\n  r2 = runBranchT[Lam, b[[1]], b[[2]], ph, nMaxN, {1, 0}]; r1 = resN[k]; dD = r1[\"D0\"];\n  ok = And @@ Table[Union[Table[rd[r1[\"series\"][nm][[n + 1]] - r2[\"series\"][nm][[n + 1]] r1[\"th12\"]^(n - If[StringTake[nm, 1] == \"b\", 2, 1])], {n, 0, nMaxN}]] === {0}, {nm, opNames}];\n  ckB[k] = Append[ckB[k], \"scal\" -> ok]], {k, Keys[ckB]}];\nck[\"B3 numeric: theta-scaling of all six series, all orders, vs theta=(1,0)\"] = And @@ Table[ckB[k][\"scal\"], {k, Keys[ckB]}];\n(* symbolic phi to order nSym *)\nnSym = 3; pphi = {p1, p2, p3}; resS = <||>; tS = <||>;\nDo[Do[Module[{b = bb, r, Lam = Lam0, rA, rB, dd0},\n  tS[{Lam, b}] = First@AbsoluteTiming[r = runBranchT[Lam, b[[1]], b[[2]], pphi, nSym, thN]]; resS[{Lam, b}] = r; dd0 = r[\"D0\"]; dD = dd0;\n  ck[{Lam, b, \"symbolic series (orders 0..\" <> ToString[nSym] <> \") == numeric at phiA and phiB, eigen-eqs exact, relations exact\"}] = And @@ Flatten[{r[\"eigOK\"], r[\"ev0\"], Table[Union[Flatten[Table[rd /@ Expand[(r[\"series\"][nm] /. Thread[pphi -> ph[[2]]]) - Take[resN[{Lam, b, ph[[1]]}][\"series\"][nm], nSym + 1]], {nm, opNames}]]] === {0}, {ph, {{\"A\", phiA}, {\"B\", phiB}}}], Table[Union[relRes[Lam, b[[1]], pphi, r, s, nSym]] === {0}, {s, 2}]}]], {bb, branchesOf[Lam0]}], {Lam0, repList}];\ndump[Join[{N[Values[tS], 3]}, List @@@ Normal[ck] /. {a_, b_} :> {ToString[a], b}]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"953927\" data-output-id=\"5\" data-out-n=\"112\" data-sub-idx=\"12\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"13\" data-sub-start=\"18\" data-sub-end=\"18\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[112]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><pre class=\"vscode-wolfram-text-output\">No output at Out[112]</pre></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[112]= No output at Out[112]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "f8084bce-59f4-4287-89be-ccd141e84ab1"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Data files `ref/laurent-series-<l1><l2><l3>.txt` (series part; the E5/XVEC/PSI records are appended after B3b)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "checks = Join[checks, ck]; ck = <||>;\nfmt[x_] := StringReplace[ToString[x, InputForm, PageWidth -> Infinity], {\"\\n\" -> \"\", \" \" -> \"\"}];\npairOf[x_] := {Coefficient[x, sq, 0], Coefficient[x, sq, 1]};\nserPairs[l_] := pairOf /@ l;\ncleanSym[x_, dd_] := If[dd === 0, Collect[Expand[x], pphi, Factor], Collect[Expand[x /. sq -> Sqrt[dd]], pphi, Simplify]];\nhdrLines[Lam_] := {\n \"# laurent-series-\" <> StringJoin[ToString /@ Lam] <> \".txt   (agent W5, notebook Paul/Mathematica/Gaudin/Experiments/Gaudin-Laurent-series.wb, 2026-10-16)\",\n \"# Exact epsilon-series of the Laurent data of the two-site gl(3) Gaudin chain, Lambda = \" <> fmt[Lam] <> \" on both sites, TWISTED with zeta = eps*phi (zeta = diag twist g = eps*phi), theta = (2/7,-3/5) (theta12 = 31/35) unless stated.\",\n \"# FORMAT: TAB-separated records, first field = tag, every other field a Wolfram InputForm expression without spaces; lines starting with # are comments. Same conventions as untwisted-exact-*.txt (W4): GT basis, site-2 = highest weight index 1, S2 = e2(zeta) + Sum_s [H_s/(u-th_s) + c2/(u-th_s)^2], S3 = e3(zeta) + Sum_s [b_s/(u-th_s) + a_s/(u-th_s)^2], c2 = lam2(lam1+1).\",\n \"# BRANCH LABELLING: a branch = (mu, copy): mu = total weight of the HW state in V(x)V (list), copy = 1 (or 2 in multiplicity-2 sectors: the two universal copies of untwisted-exact-*.txt, eigenvectors of A1 = theta12*a_1 on the HW space in Q(Sqrt[D0]); copy 1 = SMALLER a_1 at eps=0 (alpha_1 = tr/2 - f*Sqrt[D0]/2), copy 2 = larger). The branch is the eigenvector of the commuting twisted family tending to that HW vector (G-norm-normalisation irrelevant here).\",\n \"# Pair notation {p,q} = p + q*Sqrt[D0] (D0 squarefree; D0 = 0 means rational, q = 0). The octet-like sectors with mult 2 have D0 in {105,192} for Lambda=[3,1,0] mu=(5,2,1),(4,3,1) and Lambda=[3,2,0] mu=(5,4,1),(5,3,2).\",\n \"# E4_SERIES mu copy D0 phi nmax {H1,H2} {a1,a2} {b1,b2} : each of the six lists has nmax+1 pairs {p,q} = coefficients of eps^0..eps^nmax of H_s(eps), a_s(eps), b_s(eps). phi is one of the two numeric twist directions phiA=(1/3,-2/7,5/11), phiB=(-2/5,3/8,7/11). Exact facts verified on every record: H1+H2 = eps*Sum_{i!=j} phi_i mu_j (order 1 only); b1+b2 = eps^2 (phi1 phi2 mu3 + phi1 phi3 mu2 + phi2 phi3 mu1); no-log relations (b_s = a_s(H_s-a_s)/c2 for [2,1,0],[3,1,0], c2 = 3, 4; for [3,2,0] the inhomogeneous quadratic of W3 (Gaudin-L2-chain-320.wb, task B3, with W = phi.mu eps)); scaling in theta: order-n coefficient of H_s,a_s ~ theta12^(n-1), b_s ~ theta12^(n-2).\",\n \"# E4_SYMBOLIC mu copy D0 name {order0,...,order\" <> ToString[nSym] <> \"} : the same series with symbolic phi = (p1,p2,p3) as InputForm strings (name = H1,H2,a1,a2,b1,b2); Sqrt[D0] appears only for mult-2 copies.\"};\nwriteSeriesFile[Lam_] := Module[{lines = hdrLines[Lam], add, th = {2/7, -3/5}},\n  add[tag_, args__] := AppendTo[lines, StringRiffle[Prepend[fmt /@ {args}, tag], \"\\t\"]];\n  add[\"REP\", Lam]; add[\"THETA\", th]; add[\"NMAX\", nMaxN]; add[\"NSYM\", nSym];\n  add[\"BRANCHES\", Table[{b[[1]], b[[2]]}, {b, branchesOf[Lam]}]];\n  Do[Module[{mu = b[[1]], ic = b[[2]], bd = branchData[Lam, mu][[b[[2]]]]},\n    Do[Module[{pp = pq[[1]], phi = pq[[2]], r},\n      r = resN[{Lam, b, pp}]; dD = r[\"D0\"];\n      add[\"E4_SERIES\", mu, ic, dD, phi, nMaxN, {serPairs[r[\"series\"][\"H1\"]], serPairs[r[\"series\"][\"H2\"]]}, {serPairs[r[\"series\"][\"a1\"]], serPairs[r[\"series\"][\"a2\"]]}, {serPairs[r[\"series\"][\"b1\"]], serPairs[r[\"series\"][\"b2\"]]}]], {pq, {{\"A\", phiA}, {\"B\", phiB}}}];\n    Module[{rs = resS[{Lam, b}]},\n     dD = rs[\"D0\"];\n     Do[AppendTo[lines, StringRiffle[{\"E4_SYMBOLIC\", fmt[mu], fmt[ic], fmt[dD], nm, fmt[ToString[InputForm[cleanSym[#, dD]]] & /@ rs[\"series\"][nm]] }, \"\\t\"]], {nm, opNames}]]], {b, branchesOf[Lam]}];\n  Export[refDir <> \"laurent-series-\" <> StringJoin[ToString /@ Lam] <> \".txt\", StringRiffle[lines, \"\\n\"] <> \"\\n\", \"Text\"]; Length[lines]];\nnl = Table[Lam -> writeSeriesFile[Lam], {Lam, {{3, 1, 0}, {3, 2, 0}}}];\n(* the adjoint file too, a cheap cross-check against W4's E4_SERIES records *)\nnl = Append[nl, {2, 1, 0} -> writeSeriesFile[{2, 1, 0}]];\ndump[nl]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<details class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">8 warnings</summary><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Part::partw: Part 1 of {} does not exist.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Part::partw: Part 1 of {} does not exist.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Part::partd: Part specification Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][eta][[1,1,1]] is longer than depth of object.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Part::partw: Part 2 of Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][eta] does not exist.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">General::stop: Further output of Part::partw will be suppressed during this calculation.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Part::partd: Part specification Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][A][[1,1,1]] is longer than depth of object.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Part::partd: Part specification Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][B][[1,1,1]] is longer than depth of object.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">General::stop: Further output of Part::partd will be suppressed during this calculation.</div></details>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Part::partw: Part 1 of {} does not exist.\nPart::partw: Part 1 of {} does not exist.\nPart::partd: Part specification Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][eta][[1,1,1]] is longer than depth of object.\nPart::partw: Part 2 of Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][eta] does not exist.\nGeneral::stop: Further output of Part::partw will be suppressed during this calculation.\nPart::partd: Part specification Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][A][[1,1,1]] is longer than depth of object.\nPart::partd: Part specification Missing[KeyAbsent, {{3, 1, 0}, mu}][B][[1,1,1]] is longer than depth of object.\nGeneral::stop: Further output of Part::partd will be suppressed during this calculation.",
       "mime": "text/plain"
