   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary (agent W5, 2026-10-16)\n\n**B3.** Exact eps-series of (H_s, a_s, b_s) for all 6 + 10 + 10 HW-limit branches of [2,1,0], [3,1,0], [3,2,0], numeric twist phi_A = (1/3,-2/7,5/11) and phi_B = (-2/5,3/8,7/11) to order eps^10 (exact rationals, Q(Sqrt[105]), Q(Sqrt[192]), Q(Sqrt[5]) for the mult-2 copies), symbolic phi to order 3 (all branches, <= 8 s each). Isolating operator H1 + a1/7 separates every branch at eps = 0 (minimal gap 1.08). Checks, all True on every branch and both phi: eigen-equations of all six Laurent operators exact; eps^0 = W4 untwisted data; H1 + H2 = eps Sum_{i!=j} phi_i mu_j (order 1 only); b1 + b2 = eps^2 (phi1 phi2 mu3 + phi1 phi3 mu2 + phi2 phi3 mu1) (holds for all three reps); no-log relations order by order on both sites (b = a(H-a)/c2 for [2,1,0], [3,1,0]; the W3 quadratic D2 relation for [3,2,0], W = phi.mu eps); theta-scaling H_n, a_n ~ theta12^(n-1), b_n ~ theta12^(n-2) vs theta = (1,0); symbolic series == numeric at phi_A, phi_B.\n\n**Operator structure (new).** H1(zeta) = H1(0) + Sum_i zeta_i (|Lam| - E^(1)_ii) EXACTLY (no zeta^2, zeta^3 terms) as an operator on every HW weight sector; H1(0) = (|Lam|^2 + cas2(Lam) - C2^tot/2)/theta12; a1 is linear in zeta, b1 quadratic. So chi_B = det(lambda - A - eps B), a linear pencil.\n\n**B3b.** k_B = 2(l1-l3) - (mu1-mu3) on all 26 branches at both phi (adjoint 0,1,1,2,2,4; [3,1,0] 0,1,1,2,2,2,3,3,4,5; [3,2,0] 0,1,2,1,2,2,3,3,4,5, in the sector orders of the data files); x(zeta) polynomial homogeneous of degree l2; symbolic leading coefficient X_B for every branch (E5_KB records), reproduces the numeric leads.\n\n**C3.** d_B = dim C_B = dimension of the weight-mu space of V(x)V for every branch of all three reps, EXCEPT the adjoint singlet (2,2,2): d = 8 of 10 (the full char poly of H1 there is (linear factor)^2 x (irreducible degree 8); the two missing dimensions are a decoupled doubly degenerate H1 eigenvalue linear in eps). chi_B (exact, interpolated from 3d+5 rational eps, spare points exact) is irreducible over Q(eps) (Q(eps, Sqrt[D0]) for copies), annihilates the branch series to eps^10, and equals det(lambda - H1(eps)) on the weight space (checked at 4 eps per branch). The algebra generated by H1, a1 has the same cyclic subspace as H1 alone (dAlg = dA) and as all six Laurent operators (dFull = dA).\n\n**C2.** For the d = 2 branches (adjoint (4,1,1), (3,3,0); [3,1,0] (6,1,1), (5,3,0); [3,2,0] (6,3,1), (5,5,0)): in the basis (HW ket, G-orthogonal partner = weight-mu vector of the neighbouring irrep nu = mu + e_i - e_j) H1 = (1/2) Sum_{i!=j} zeta_i mu_j + [[eta_mu/theta12, (zeta_j - zeta_i)/2], [(zeta_j - zeta_i)/2, eta_nu/theta12]] (exact symbolic in z1,z2,z3,theta12), so H1 = (1/2) Sum_{i!=j} zeta_i mu_j + (eta_mu + eta_nu)/(2 theta12) +- Sqrt[((eta_mu - eta_nu)/(2 theta12))^2 + (zeta_i - zeta_j)^2/4]; and a1 = alpha + beta H1 with beta = c2 (top-adjacent type) or 0.\n\n**Duality.** [3,2,0] = [3,1,0]* (x) det^3: mu -> mu' = (6-mu3, 6-mu2, 6-mu1), zeta -> zeta' = -(zeta3, zeta2, zeta1); the multiplicity-2 copies swap (copy 1 <-> copy 2). H1'(zeta') = H1(zeta) + 6/theta12 - 6 Sum zeta; H2' = H2 - 6/theta12 - 6 Sum zeta; a1' = 4 H1 - a1 - 24/theta12 - 12 Sum zeta; a2' = 4 H2 - a2 + 24/theta12 - 12 Sum zeta (exact on all 10 branches, all orders to 10, phi_A); b follows from the no-log relations.\n\n**Data files.** `Paul/Mathematica/Gaudin/ref/laurent-series-{210,310,320}.txt` (E4_SERIES, E4_SYMBOLIC, E5_KB, E5_KBNUM, XVEC, PSI, GNORM).\n\n**Mode.** Native outputs stored for the first cells; all printed results of later cells were read through scratch dump files (tool channel truncates long messages).",
